# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull request touches. For a
# repository with one maintainer that is mostly a way of never missing a contribution:
# the request lands in one place whether somebody fixes a typo or rewrites the tenancy
# layer.
#
# The later a rule appears, the more it wins — the last matching pattern for a file is the
# one that applies, not the union of all of them. So the catch-all goes first.
#
# Ownership here is about attention, not permission. What a pull request is allowed to do
# is decided by branch protection and by the tests, not by this file.

